# vdefaultdelivery file for vpopmail
#
# This file is interpreted by vdelvermail whenever an address has no lines defined
# in the valias table.
# It uses the same syntax as .qmail files, as does valias database table.
# Multiple lines are possible.
# https://manpages.debian.org/buster/qmail/dot-qmail.5.en.html
# 
# Note that pipe commands below are forked and passed to /bin/sh, so you can utilise
# environment variables provided by qmail-local. Put quotes around them all.
# See https://manpages.debian.org/buster/qmail/qmail-command.8.en.html
#   $PATH - whatever was given to qmail-start
#   $EXT - local part of the recipient address
#   $HOST - the domain name from the recipient address
#   $USER - the dealiased domain name of the recipient address. It's dealised using users/assign.
#   $SENDER - obtained from the mail queue via queue/intd/<inode> , which is different to the message file itself.
# Some aspects of that man page don't apply here, e.g. the current directory is actually
# the recipient's mailbox directory from vpopmail.pw_dir in the db.
# Your pipe commands should add "Delivered-To" and "Return-Path" whenever they do final
# delivery, or even forwarding via qmail-inject.
# It's OK that some maildir files will contain more than one Delivered-To and Return-Path header.

# deliver with dovecot-lda
# |/var/qmail/bin/preline -f /usr/local/dovecot/libexec/dovecot/deliver -d $EXT@$USER 

./Maildir/
